WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.900
Arize Phoenix.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:06.833
Open-source tracing and evaluation that launches right inside a notebook.

3
00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:10.367
Phoenix is built OpenTelemetry-native.

4
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:14.100
It ingests standard spans through the OpenInference conventions.

5
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.100
So anything you already instrumented flows straight in.

6
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.233
What sets it apart from a generic trace viewer is the analysis layer.

7
00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:25.700
Traces show every retrieve, rerank, and model call.

8
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.100
Retrieval analysis shows which documents each query pulled, and how relevant they were.

9
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.300
Embedding drift projects query and document clusters over time.

10
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.767
And evals run inside the same tool.

11
00:00:38.967 --> 00:00:40.700
Think of how it fits with Langfuse.

12
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.000
OTel is the shared base, so you don't choose at instrumentation time.

13
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.200
Phoenix is the open-a-debugger tool for RAG work.

14
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.267
Langfuse is the run-it-in-production counterpart.

15
00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:54.133
Here's how small the barrier is.

16
00:00:54.433 --> 00:00:56.542
One call launches a local UI.

17
00:00:56.542 --> 00:00:58.433
No docker, and no account.

18
00:00:58.733 --> 00:01:01.833
One line instruments your framework, so traces flow in.

19
00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:06.467
Run some queries, then open the traces, retrieval, and embeddings views.

20
00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.667
Here's a story.

21
00:01:08.967 --> 00:01:14.533
Mission Control's retrieval quality quietly degrades, and RAGAS says so, but not why.

22
00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:17.772
You load two thousand traced queries into Phoenix.

23
00:01:17.772 --> 00:01:22.767
The corpus cluster hasn't moved, but a new lobe of queries has grown off to the side.

24
00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:27.652
Users started asking about the Artemis logs, which were never ingested.

25
00:01:27.652 --> 00:01:29.202
Retrieval wasn't broken.

26
00:01:29.202 --> 00:01:30.558
The corpus was stale.

27
00:01:30.558 --> 00:01:33.400
One picture ended a week of prompt tweaking.

28
00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:35.421
Let's recap.

29
00:01:35.421 --> 00:01:38.567
Phoenix is OTel-native tracing and evaluation.

30
00:01:38.867 --> 00:01:42.167
It adds retrieval analysis and embedding drift views.

31
00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:44.833
It launches in a notebook with a single call.

32
00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:48.577
Use it as your debugger, and Langfuse for production.

33
00:01:48.577 --> 00:01:50.267
Next up: diffusion models.
